{
  "version": 1,
  "spec": "HISTORY_SPEC.md",
  "description": "history() full-depth 'logs' strategy with the windowed, bounded-prefetch logs pass. Chain height 4,999,999 with logsWindow 2,000,000 yields exactly three windows, scanned newest-first. The newest window holds one incoming USDT transfer, the middle window is empty, the oldest holds one outgoing USDT transfer. concurrency 2 means the third window may only be requested after the first completes.",
  "notes": [
    "bigint values are decimal strings; convert before comparing.",
    "tokenTransfers[].tokens is a JSON object {tokenId: value}; the real value is Map<bigint, bigint> ('1' is the fixed ERC-20 id).",
    "eth_getLogs calls are matched by (topics, fromBlock, toBlock); any call not listed in rpc.eth_getLogs.responses must be answered with [].",
    "blockTimestamp on txs/logs is the erigon extension; receipts intentionally omit timestamp so HistoryTx.timestamp exercises the info.blockTimestamp fallback."
  ],
